<h2>What actually happens</h2>
<ul class="checks">
  <li>The app reads your public RSS feed, like any other player.</li>
  <li>The listener downloads the file <strong>from your server</strong>, directly. The download is counted on your side.</li>
  <li>We keep no copy. No proxy, no CDN of ours, no storage.</li>
  <li>Ads that your server inserts dynamically stay exactly as your server delivered them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the processing does</h2>
<p>Volume levelling between speakers, on the device, while listening. It doesn't change your file and isn't stored anywhere. It's the equivalent of a listener turning the volume knob, only automatic.</p>

<h2>If you'd rather not</h2>
<p>Send us the show's name and feed address, and we'll remove it from the app. No questions, no conditions.</p>
